  "term": "empirical validity",
  "definition": "Empirical validity is the extent to which a measure is supported by observed data, such as whether it shows the expected statistical relationship with the outcomes it is supposed to help explain or predict. In this packet, it refers to judging a measure by how well it performs in real-world analyses compared with alternative measures.",
