      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s general characterization of empirical validity as “the extent to which a measure is supported by observed data” and specifically whether it “shows the expected statistical relationship” is not explicitly stated or defined anywhere in the packet text; the packet instead describes a particular study approach (comparing empirical associations in tract-level cross-sectional models).",
        "The packet supports that, in this context, the authors assess the SVI’s empirical associations and compare it with an alternative measure (CDI), but it does not provide the broader, generic statement in the first sentence about “expected statistical relationship” with outcomes a measure is “supposed to help explain or predict.”"
